SDAQ: SENEB), the full-vote Class B shares of one of North America's largest fruit/vegetable processors, controlling distribution in retail private-label canned vegetables, foodservice, and export, and owner of Green Giant (shelf-stable and, as of March 2026, U.S. frozen).\n\n**T0 snapshot:**\n- SENEB price: $195.39 | SENEB shares out: 6,770,500 | SENEB market cap: $1.323B [Aggregator, Actual]\n- Total company shares: ~6.98M (wtd-avg diluted FY2025, [Filed]); SENEA residual ~0.21M [Estimate] \u2192 Equity value ~$1.36B [Estimate]\n- Net debt: ~$232M [Estimate; vendor total debt $282M \u2212 vendor cash $50M, both [Aggregator] for the last annual report]\n- Enterprise value: ~$1.59B [Estimate]\n\n**Headline conclusion:** The company is a quality *cyclical* \u2014 dominant in an unattractive, thin-margin category \u2014 exiting an input-cost trough into a margin peak (FY2026 gross margin 13.9%, the highest in the 12-year filed window). The stock at $195 is paying 11.4x **peak** TTM earnings and embeds a permanently sustainable ~6.0% operating margin. History says margins mean-revert; the 12-year median operating margin is ~5.1%. Probability-weighted intrinsic value: **\u2248$150/share**. Margin of safety: **\u2248 \u221230% (None). Action: SELL / DO NOT BUY.** No short recommended for operational (borrow/float) reasons.\n\n**Data reliability warning:** The acquisition price of the Green Giant U.S. frozen business was **not disclosed**; its revenue contribution is an **assumption** built from B&G's segment disclosures. The pack itself warns that multi-year trends may contain basis changes, and the quarterly table omits the 2026-03-31 quarter. Where inputs are not from filings, they are tagged.\n\n**Model confidence: MODERATE-LOW.** Tiers 4-5 drive the critical swing variables (normalized margin, acquisition contribution).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u