e 27, 2026) 10-Q filed Aug 6, 2026 [Actual]\n\n**Scope**: Seneca Foods Corporation, class B common (SENEB). Class A (SENEA) trades at $176.30 vs B at $195.39 as of T0 \u2014 a 10.8% price divergence attributable to liquidity/preference effects, not economics. I am analyzing the equity on an as-converted, per-share economic basis. **[Actual]**\n\n**Filing basis**: FY2026 annual results released June 11, 2026: net sales $1,659.7M; gross margin 13.9% vs 9.5% prior year; record FIFO diluted EPS $14.15. **[Actual \u2014 company press release]** Q1 FY2027 (June 27, 2026): net sales $405.2M vs $297.5M (+36.2%, includes Green Giant Frozen); FIFO EBITDA $38.0M vs $25.2M; diluted EPS $2.85 vs $2.14. **[Actual \u2014 10-Q/press release]**\n\n**Historical pack note**: The FY2016 step-up in revenue to $1.280B (from $1.286B) and gross profit $151M is anomalous vs adjacent years \u2014 likely a one-time inventory liquidation gain rather than a business event. Pack section 0 continuity warning applies. I treat FY2017 as the base for margin normalization, not FY2016. **[Estimate \u2014 basis-change judgment per pack warning]**\n\n**Key disclosed event**: On March 2, 2026, Seneca closed the purchase of the Green Giant U.S. frozen business (brand/IP, inventory, Yuma AZ plant) from B&G Foods. Terms undisclosed. **[Actual \u2014 both companies' press releases]**\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 1. Macro Context\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u25